Package: FoSci
Title: Forensic Scientometrics: Integrity Signals in Publication Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Detects statistical and textual signals that may deserve a
    closer look in collections of scientific publications, and documents
    the evidence behind them: retraction rates, journal-to-journal citation
    stacking, template titles, tortured phrases (Cabanac, Labbe and
    Magazinov, 2021, <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2107.06751>) and unusual
    productivity, with a module for paper mill screening. Every result
    carries an evidence level (signal, pattern, documentary, established)
    and its alternative explanations; a signal is never presented as proof
    of misconduct, and individuals are not ranked. Reads 'OpenAlex'
    <https://openalex.org/> responses and the 'Retraction Watch' database,
    includes a simulated benchmark with known outcomes to validate the
    methods, and writes reproducible case reports.
